  "title": "A Sharp Nonattained Clique-Web Ratio on a Three-Parameter Lorentzian Family",
  "batch_label": "57",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For all positive real r,q,t satisfying r+q-2 >= sqrt(5)|r-q| and t^2 >= (1+2r+2q)/5, the supremum of P(r,q,t)^alpha=(q/t^2)^(5/4) is ((5+sqrt(5))/4)^(5/4). No finite feasible triple attains the supremum. For every integer n>=1, q_n=n, r_n=((sqrt(5)-1)+(3-sqrt(5))n)/2, and t_n=sqrt((sqrt(5)+(5-sqrt(5))n)/5) form a feasible exact sequence whose objective values converge to that supremum. The scope is only the frozen displayed three-parameter family and asserts nothing about equality with the global constant f(alpha).",
